WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.930 --> 00:00:09.163
- That would make me
less mad about traffic.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:15.085
Welcome, Bobby.
- Thank, thank you.

00:00:15.085 --> 00:00:17.050
- Thanks so much for being here.

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:20.240
Bobby is the interior
designer extraordinaire

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.650
on Netflix hit show Queer Eye.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:25.170
Today, we have some audience questions

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.070
on how to make their spaces better.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:28.200
- Thanks for sending these in, guys.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:29.250
I won't be too harsh.

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.040
- Hello, my name is Abby.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:32.650
I am in my craft room right now.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:35.080
- I would love help making my craft room

00:00:35.080 --> 00:00:37.140
feel more creative and inspiring.

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:41.260
What I would recommend is paint
something cool on the wall.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:44.170
If you're not a good
painter, do a geometric.

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:45.680
You know, squares, circles, triangles,

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:46.710
those are always very easy.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:48.140
Doing cool, bright colors,

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:50.440
I think that would definitely
make it feel more inspiring

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.658
and more of a creative space.
- I like that!

00:00:52.658 --> 00:00:53.491
- Hi, guys.

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:54.689
My name's Rebecca.

00:00:54.689 --> 00:00:56.630
- This random room in our house

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.590
has a fabulous view of our backyard,

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:00.080
but nothing we do with it sticks.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:02.290
Now it's just extra space
for our new baby stuff.

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:05.160
It also opens up to our backyard
where we let the dog out.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.943
So, bedroom is not the best option.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:08.230
If it has space for the outdoors,

00:01:08.230 --> 00:01:09.390
definitely make it a space

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:11.490
where you can appreciate
the view of the outdoors.

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:13.100
Put a nice little sofa or chair,

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.721
make it a little reading room maybe.

00:01:14.721 --> 00:01:16.797
- Add a little bar cart.
- Yeah, definitely

00:01:16.797 --> 00:01:19.703
for a nice little martini in
the afternoon and a good read.

00:01:19.703 --> 00:01:23.360
- My husband and I just
moved into our own place

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:25.790
and it's a basement.

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:27.820
- And I would like some tips
on making it feel more homey,

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:29.893
less 70s, and not feel as dark.

00:01:29.981 --> 00:01:31.240
I actually like the room.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.240
I think it looks groovy,

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:34.024
but if you're wanting
it to not feel so dark,

00:01:34.024 --> 00:01:35.690
I would paint the walls white.

00:01:35.690 --> 00:01:37.140
It will really open up the space.

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:39.093
Maybe keep the bar there, though,

00:01:39.093 --> 00:01:41.402
so that way it adds a
little bit of depth to it.

00:01:41.402 --> 00:01:43.237
As Johnathan would say, meow!

00:01:44.175 --> 00:01:45.417
- Hi, friends, I'm Natalie,

00:01:45.417 --> 00:01:46.760
and my interior design question

00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:50.090
is about maximizing the
space I have in my kitchen

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.923
slash dining area that's
all kind of one thing.

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:56.830
I would probably do mounted
cabinets up on the upper walls

00:01:56.830 --> 00:01:58.510
so that way you can still
sit at the dining table,

00:01:58.510 --> 00:01:59.590
but you have upper storage.

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:01.030
It'll actually make the room feel larger

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:01.863
'cause it'll draw your eye up.

00:02:01.863 --> 00:02:03.850
- I live in a university residence.

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:06.240
All of our rooms look
like ugly jail cells.

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:07.660
- Looking for ways to brighten my room

00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:08.900
and make it feel like home.

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:11.390
My advice in dorms is removable wallpaper

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.150
because most dorms I
know won't let you paint.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.830
It's a good way to give
it some personality,

00:02:14.830 --> 00:02:15.892
make it feel more like home

00:02:15.892 --> 00:02:18.199
without getting in
trouble with the school.

00:02:18.199 --> 00:02:19.671
- I wanna maximize my space

00:02:19.671 --> 00:02:22.270
so I can have friends come over and visit.

00:02:22.270 --> 00:02:23.823
- The problem is it's a micro-efficiency

00:02:23.823 --> 00:02:27.283
measuring under 150 square feet, tiny.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.310
- You can always have
friends over, though.

00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.050
- I would move the desk over
a little more towards the bed

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:34.400
and it will double as a
desk and a night stand,

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:35.450
and then under that window,

00:02:35.450 --> 00:02:37.670
I would do a storage bench
with a cushion on top.

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:40.830
And that way it adds
storage in your small place,

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:43.160
but it also makes for basically
a sofa over in the corner.

00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:43.993
- I love that.

00:02:43.993 --> 00:02:45.100
- My name is Bailey.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.580
Thank you so much for taking the time

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.960
to listen to my sad decorating woes.

00:02:48.960 --> 00:02:50.960
- I have always been bad at decorating

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:53.350
or knowing anything about how
to make a house or a home.

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:56.383
The only thing I refuse to
take down is my Irish flag,

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.410
but please, for the love of
all that is holy, please help.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:01.720
I would actually hang
the flag over the bed,

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.560
kind of make it as a headboard.

00:03:03.560 --> 00:03:05.780
Get some bedding that
coordinates with the flag.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:06.915
If you're gonna go for it, go for it.

00:03:06.915 --> 00:03:08.270
Make it a theme.
- Go full Irish.

00:03:08.270 --> 00:03:09.530
- A good old Irish theme.

00:03:09.530 --> 00:03:11.780
- Yeah, I feel like every
time I get new bedding,

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:14.089
it makes me just feel
happier and refreshed.

00:03:14.089 --> 00:03:16.320
- Bedding is something
you should splurge on.

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:17.720
You wanna wake up feelin' happy.

00:03:17.720 --> 00:03:19.130
You wanna go to bed feeling happy.

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.860
Spend a little extra
money on good bedding.

00:03:20.860 --> 00:03:22.760
Don't be fooled by the
whole thread count thing,

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:23.740
it's not real.
- Really?

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:24.985
- It's an American marketing ploy.

00:03:24.985 --> 00:03:27.170
(gasps)
- If it feels good, it's good.

00:03:27.170 --> 00:03:28.290
If it doesn't feel nice,

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.530
no matter how many thread
count or how expensive it is,

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:31.641
it's not nice.

00:03:31.641 --> 00:03:32.474
- So, that's it.

00:03:32.474 --> 00:03:33.375
Thank you so much

00:03:33.375 --> 00:03:34.830
for stopping by.
- Of course, no, it was fun.

00:03:34.830 --> 00:03:36.763
- Where can people follow
you on your socials?

00:03:36.763 --> 00:03:39.870
- You can follow me @bobbyberk
on Instagram or Twitter.

00:03:39.870 --> 00:03:41.230
- Be sure to check out Bobby

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:44.063
and let us know if you
have any more questions.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:47.973
(upbeat music)

00:03:54.930 --> 00:03:56.950
- Hey, Unsolved is on a new
channel, and now your part.

00:03:56.950 --> 00:03:58.153
- [Both] Subscribe here.

00:03:58.190 --> 00:03:59.140
- That was my part.

